## How to judge
1. Re-run every acceptance-criterion command yourself. Compare with what the builder pasted.
2. Read the diff of this wave (git diff {{.WaveBase}}..HEAD). Look for: criteria met only
   in letter, tests that assert nothing, disabled or skipped tests, hard-coded outputs,
   read-only paths touched, rule violations, and claims with no pasted output.
3. A defect is BLOCKING if an acceptance criterion does not hold or a rule is broken.
   Minor issues that do not block go under "Deferred" and do not stop VERIFIED.

## Your final message — exactly this shape
### Re-run
Each command you ran and what it actually printed.
### Defects
One per line, numbered, most important first, blocking ones only:
D1: <one-line headline> — <file/test> — <what fails and how to see it>
(write "none" if there are none)
### Deferred
Non-blocking notes.

The very last line must be exactly one of:
VERDICT: VERIFIED   (every acceptance criterion re-ran green, no blocking defects)
VERDICT: REWORK     (at least one blocking defect listed above)
VERDICT: ESCALATE   (a human must decide — the rules or the wave itself look wrong; say why)
